@page "/virtualized"

<PageTitle>Virtualize + KeepRegistered</PageTitle>
<h1>Virtualize + KeepRegistered</h1>
<p>200 rows in a virtualized container. KeepRegistered keeps scrolled-away rows revealed, so submit still reports their errors — and the summary's focus fallback scrolls far rows into view on click.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "Virtualized.razor", "Virtualized.razor.cs", "GadgetOrder.cs" })">
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li>Every row's <strong>Serial</strong> is required (live). Every 7th row starts empty.</li>
            <li><code>KeepRegistered</code> keeps scrolled-away rows disclosed, so their errors stay in the summary.</li>
            <li>The summary's <code>FocusFallback</code> handles rows outside the render window: scroll the panel to the row, let Virtualize render it, retry the focus once.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Submit — the summary lists errors including rows far outside the viewport.</li>
            <li>Click an entry near the top — it focuses directly.</li>
            <li>Click one of the LAST entries — the panel scrolls, the row renders, and focus lands. That is the fallback at work.</li>
            <li>Fix a serial, scroll far away, submit again — the row's verdict updates without it being visible.</li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
</TeachingPanel>

<FormidableForm Model="_order" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid">
    <FormSummary FocusFallback="ScrollToRowAsync" />

    <div class="scroll-panel">
        <Virtualize Items="_order.Gadgets" ItemSize="RowHeight" Context="gadget">
            <div class="field" @key="gadget">
                <label>Serial
                    <FormidableInputText For="() => gadget.Serial" @bind-Value="gadget.Serial" KeepRegistered="true" />
                </label>
                <FieldMessage For="() => gadget.Serial" />
            </div>
        </Virtualize>
    </div>

    <div class="actions"><button type="submit">Submit</button></div>
</FormidableForm>

<p role="status">@_status</p>
